<title>SWITZERLAND: Oerlikon posts higher 1996 net profit.</title>
<headline>Oerlikon posts higher 1996 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calender 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net after min	  62		  vs 3</p>
<p> Group net before min	 61		  vs 4</p>
<p> Operating result	     204		 vs 139</p>
<p> Div per reg'd (Sfr)	  1.20		vs 0</p>
<p>NOTE - Company said it was proposing first dividend since one paid on 1985 results.  Sales			    3,613	     vs 3,814</p>
<p> Operating result	     204		 vs 139</p>
<p> Orders received		3,531	     vs 3,741</p>
<p> Orders on hand		 2,137	     vs 2,283</p>
<p> Financial result	     75 loss	   vs 71 loss</p>
<p> Extraordinary result	 7 loss	    vs 28 loss</p>
<p> Taxes			    61		  vs 36</p>
<p> Net debt			 1,174	     vs 1,276</p>
<p> Payroll			  15,543	    vs 17,118</p>
<p>NOTE - Arms-to-fashion group Oerlikon-Buehrle Holding AG said it was recovering from the previous year's setback, when net profit plunged from 75 million to three million Swiss francs. A company statement said it was now on the right track with a concentrated portfolio.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
